Restore the upstream guard before initializing the RandR extension.

Xnest does not initialize RandR on any screen. Removing this guard lets
RRClientCallback run with the screen private key unregistered, causing
an assertion when the first client connects. Restoring the upstream
precondition prevents the extension from using uninitialized state.

Revert the XQuartz-specific change:
https://github.com/XQuartz/xorg-server/commit/535a649c0b7d2a1cf2ed5c3d41a78502c4f217d3

Historical discussion:
https://lists.x.org/archives/xorg-devel/2016-October/051580.html

Upstream report:
https://github.com/XQuartz/XQuartz/issues/517

--- a/randr/randr.c
+++ b/randr/randr.c
@@ -414,6 +414,9 @@
 {
     ExtensionEntry *extEntry;

+    if (RRNScreens == 0)
+        return;
+
     if (!dixRegisterPrivateKey(&RRClientPrivateKeyRec, PRIVATE_CLIENT,
                                sizeof(RRClientRec) +
                                screenInfo.numScreens * sizeof(RRTimesRec)))
